Z||000000||hugh||08-24-2000||09:18 PM||||I already have custom wheels on my  88,but I'm waiting for Bilstein struts from Ryane.Once they are on,I need to replace the rear tires anyway,I want to go with something like 295/50/15 tires.Is anyone using this size tire now?I will replace the wheels if I have to.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hugh_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||08-24-2000||09:49 PM||||uuuum you'd need a 9.5" wide wheel for proper fit of a 295mm tire! I had 17x8.5 with 255s on them running 310lbft of tq at 1300rpm and was VERY hard pressed to break them loose.. why do you want such a larger tire?  If your only gunna use the car on the strip and your looking for a wrinkle wall put a 295 on a 8" wheel and have 8-15lbs of air in it.. but don't drive it on the street...||||reg||1
